# Rank 1586 / CVE-2022-31018: Play Framework's JSON form binding
# recursed into nested objects and arrays with no depth limit, so a
# deeply nested JSON body threw a StackOverflowError and took the
# request thread down (denial of service through unbounded recursion,
# CWE-1327/CWE-400; PR #11301, backported to 2.8.16). doFromJson in
# core/play/src/main/scala/play/api/data/Form.scala flattened a
# JsValue into the form's key-value map by recursing at every
# JsObject/JsArray node, bounded only by the max-chars budget of the
# produced map -- nesting depth itself is unbounded. The fixing commit
# f6722f1e57 (the merge "[2.8.x] add
# depth limit for JSON form binding"): a new
# Form.FromJsonMaxDepth = 64 (an InternalApi constant), fromJson
# overloads carrying maxDepth, and the recursion throwing once its
# level exceeds the bound. .
#
# ATTENTION, recursion depth budgets. The sibling budget (maxChars)
# existed -- the depth of the walked structure is unbounded, the
# same cross-iteration budget family as ranks 1534 (header
# accumulation) and 1559 (wire length): the corpus's CWE-400 rules
# judge per-iteration progress, not a depth carried through
# recursion, so nothing can ask "does the JSON walk stop at a depth
# cap". A binding on Play's own FormUtils would detect this
# framework rather than the weakness. Measured on the real code:
# scanning Form.scala reports zero findings at both revisions. No
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the piece is depth-budget vocabulary, not a
# localised construct. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1586 records the unbounded recursion and the depth-capped
# form, both asserting reject VYQL-DOS-029: when depth-budget
# vocabulary lands, the unbounded form must flip to expect.

test "rank1586: the json walk recurses without a depth cap"
  lang scala
  file core/play/src/main/scala/play/api/data/Form.scala
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  import play.api.libs.json._

  object FormUtils {
    def fromJson(js: JsValue, maxChars: Long): Map[String, String] =
      doFromJson(Root(js), Map.empty, 0, maxChars)

    private def doFromJson(node: Node, out: Map[String, String], level: Int, maxChars: Long): Map[String, String] = {
      val result = node match {
        case Object(fields) =>
          fields.flatMap { case (key, value) =>
            doFromJson(Field(key, value), out, level + 1, maxChars)
          }.toMap
        case Array(elements) =>
          elements.zipWithIndex.flatMap { case (value, index) =>
            doFromJson(Element(index, value), out, level + 1, maxChars)
          }.toMap
        case Leaf(key, value) =>
          Map(key -> value)
      }
      result
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1586: the fixed revision caps the recursion depth"
  lang scala
  file core/play/src/main/scala/play/api/data/Form.scala
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  import play.api.libs.json._

  object FormUtils {
    final val MaxDepth: Int = 64

    def fromJson(js: JsValue, maxChars: Long, maxDepth: Int): Map[String, String] =
      doFromJson(Root(js), Map.empty, 0, maxChars, maxDepth)

    private def doFromJson(node: Node, out: Map[String, String], level: Int, maxChars: Long, maxDepth: Int): Map[String, String] = {
      if (level > maxDepth) {
        throw new RuntimeException("JSON form binding exceeded max depth")
      }
      val result = node match {
        case Object(fields) =>
          fields.flatMap { case (key, value) =>
            doFromJson(Field(key, value), out, level + 1, maxChars, maxDepth)
          }.toMap
        case Array(elements) =>
          elements.zipWithIndex.flatMap { case (value, index) =>
            doFromJson(Element(index, value), out, level + 1, maxChars, maxDepth)
          }.toMap
        case Leaf(key, value) =>
          Map(key -> value)
      }
      result
    }
  }
  ```
